  "title": "dsh replaces opencode as the third reviewer",
  "summary": "The review check's third reviewer job changes from opencode (OpenRouter) to dsh (DeepSeek). dsh gains a documented read-only mode — the `DSH_PERMISSION_MODE=read-only` environment variable — so it is no longer refused at run time, and its launch drops the `sh -c` wrapper: osf now starts `dsh --profile headless` directly and feeds the prompt on standard input. The workflow renames the job, swaps the provider secret and network allow-list entry to `api.deepseek.com`, and adds a step that fails unless the pinned image carries dsh 0.2.0-rc.2. The roster in osf.toml and the docs follow.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
